<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  PLAN 53 P4, DECISION D4 (a) (QBX-182). THE GROUP EXTENT `C_g`, AND WHAT IT
  DOES TO A MEMBER WHOSE CLIPS DO NOT FIT IT.

  D4 asked what an un-armed member's column should be when its clips cross the
  armed lane's column extent, or when two armed lanes in one group disagree
  about theirs; (a) is "the member's column extent IS the group's `C`, and
  member children crossing its edges are split there first". This case drives
  `place-recording` directly - no capture device, no transport, no wall-clock
  jitter - so every number below is a closed form, and it reaches the
  `armed="0"` path of BOTH takes planners plus the `armed="0"` no-op of the
  other two modes.

  test_sawtooth.wav is 4 s at 48 kHz = 192000 frames, which is what makes the
  arithmetic closed. Four lanes in edit group 1:

    lane 0  ARMED   clip [0, 192000)        -> its own C = [0, 192000)
    lane 1  ARMED   clip [96000, 288000)    -> its own C = [48000, 288000)
    lane 2  member  clip [0, 192000)
    lane 3  member  clip [240000, 432000)

  and ONE pass, [48000, 144000), on both armed lanes. So

    C_g = C0 u C1 = [0, 288000)

  which is wider than EITHER armed lane's own extent. That is the second half
  of D4 and the half that is easy to miss: §3.4's rule is "ONE rule for EVERY
  member, armed or not", so the group extent widens the ARMED lanes' columns
  too, and lane 0's column comes out 288000 long although nothing it holds
  reaches past 192000. Without that, lanes 0 and 1 would not be each other's
  twins either (`seditgroups::correspondingClip` matches startTime AND duration
  exactly), and a band's multi-mic take would fall out of the group on the
  first pass.

  WHAT EACH LANE ENDS UP WITH, and why:

    lane 0  column [0, 288000), takes [0-192000] and the pass [48000-144000),
            map 0 -> clip, 48000 -> pass, 144000 -> clip. The span
            [192000, 288000) is inside the COLUMN and outside every take, which
            under invariant 1' plays SILENCE - exactly what the lane played
            there before (plan 53 §3.1 step 5), so the widening is audible
            nowhere.
    lane 1  column [0, 288000), takes [96000-288000] and the pass
            [48000-144000), map 48000 -> pass, 144000 -> clip. Nothing answers
            before 48000, which is again what the lane played there before.
    lane 2  THE UNION PLACEHOLDER (§4.2, invariant 3'): a ONE-take column whose
            take covers [0, 192000) of a 288000-long column. This is the shape
            that made invariant 3 -> 3' necessary: a one-take column collapses
            to a plain cut only when its take is FULL-extent, and collapsing
            this one would move the clip's edges onto the take's and lose the
            column's own length - and with it the twin match.
    lane 3  THE CROSSING, which is what this case is named for: its clip runs
            from 240000 to 432000 and `C_g` ends at 288000, so it is SPLIT
            there first. The inside piece [240000, 288000) becomes the
            placeholder column (extent `C_g`, one take at 240000-288000) and
            the OUTSIDE piece [288000, 432000) stays a plain clip, untouched
            and un-wrapped. The split is the mode-B primitive and undoes
            cleanly, which is why D4 (a) chose it over refusing the member.

  THE TWIN KEY IS `startTime` PLUS THE OBJECT'S DURATION, and the two are
  asserted by different verbs here: `assert-clip-window startTime=` reads the
  LINK, while the length comes from `assert-take-column duration=` - the
  COLUMN's own length. `assert-clip-window duration=` on a direct column
  reports the ACTIVE TAKE's window instead, which is a different number and
  not the one `correspondingClip` matches on.

  AND THE TWO MODES THAT NEVER TOUCH A MEMBER (G9): lane 4, in its own group,
  is handed `armed="0"` under `replace` and under `overdub` and keeps its one
  plain clip - the planner's half of what `record_mode_replace_group` gates
  through the recorder. It is also handed `armed="0"` under `takes` with NO
  group extent, which is the pre-P4 meaning of the attribute and must still be
  nothing to do: that is what keeps every `place-recording` call written before
  this ticket behaving as it did.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="takes_group_record_crossing">

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <add-sample trackIndex="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="1" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="96000"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="2" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="3" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="240000"/>
    <add-sample trackIndex="4" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav" timePos="0"/>

    <set-edit-group trackPath="0" group="1"/>
    <set-edit-group trackPath="1" group="1"/>
    <set-edit-group trackPath="2" group="1"/>
    <set-edit-group trackPath="3" group="1"/>
    <set-edit-group trackPath="4" group="2"/>

    <!-- THE PASS, on the two ARMED lanes, with the group extent the recorder
         would have computed: C_g = [0, 288000). `takeStamp` is what the
         recorder puts on the take it just made; a fixed value here, because a
         wall-clock one cannot be asserted. -->
    <place-recording trackPath="0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="takes"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000" takeStamp="12:00"/>
    <place-recording trackPath="1" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="takes"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000" takeStamp="12:00"/>
    <!-- ...AND THE SAME PASS FOR THE MEMBERS, `armed="0"`: the structure and
         nothing else. The file path is the armed lanes' capture, which is what
         the recorder passes too - the verb reads it for the pass's LENGTH and
         an un-armed plan places nothing from it. -->
    <place-recording trackPath="2" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="takes" armed="0"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000"/>
    <place-recording trackPath="3" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="takes" armed="0"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000"/>

    <!-- LANE 0: the armed lane whose own C was SMALLER than the group's. Its
         column is 288000 long, not 192000. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="1"
                        extents="0-192000;48000-144000"
                        comp="0:0;48000:1;144000:0" duration="288000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takeAtPos="24000"  expectTake="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takeAtPos="72000"  expectTake="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takeAtPos="160000" expectTake="0"/>
    <!-- ...and the widened tail is SILENCE, not some take that happens to be
         nearby: the map answers take 0 there and take 0 has no material. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takeAtPos="250000" expectTake="-1"/>

    <!-- LANE 1: the other armed lane. Same extent, different takes - a group
         keeps the geometry in step, not the content. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" shape="direct" takes="2" activeTake="1"
                        extents="96000-288000;48000-144000"
                        comp="48000:1;144000:0" duration="288000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,0" startTime="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" takeAtPos="24000"  expectTake="-1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" takeAtPos="72000"  expectTake="1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" takeAtPos="200000" expectTake="0"/>

    <!-- LANE 2: THE UNION PLACEHOLDER. One take, covering two thirds of its
         own column - the shape invariant 3' exists for. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" shape="direct" takes="1" activeTake="0"
                        extents="0-192000" comp="0:0" duration="288000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,0" startTime="0"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" takeAtPos="24000"  expectTake="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" takeAtPos="250000" expectTake="-1"/>

    <!-- LANE 3: THE CROSSING. The inside piece became the placeholder column
         at `C_g`; the outside piece is still a plain clip at its own place. -->
    <assert-take-column clip="3,0" shape="direct" takes="1" activeTake="0"
                        extents="240000-288000" comp="240000:0"
                        duration="288000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="3,0" startTime="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="3,1" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="3,1" startTime="288000" duration="144000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="3,2" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="3,0" takeAtPos="100000" expectTake="-1"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="3,0" takeAtPos="260000" expectTake="0"/>

    <!-- G9, THE PLANNER'S HALF: `replace` and `overdub` do nothing at all to
         an un-armed lane, group extent or no group extent. -->
    <place-recording trackPath="4" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="replace" armed="0"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000"/>
    <place-recording trackPath="4" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="overdub" armed="0"
                     groupStart="0" groupLength="288000"/>
    <!-- ...and `armed="0"` with NO group extent is the PRE-P4 meaning,
         "nothing to do", which every call written before this ticket relies
         on. -->
    <place-recording trackPath="4" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"
                     timePos="48000" length="96000" mode="takes" armed="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="4,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="4,0" startTime="0" duration="192000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="4,1" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- UNDO: four passes, four steps (a `.qxa` submits each on its own; a
         real press wraps them in one commit scope, which
         `takes_group_record_unarmed` asserts). The three no-ops above each
         cost a step too - an empty plan applies as SUCCESS. -->
    <undo count="7"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="1,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="2,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="3,0" shape="none"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,0" startTime="0"      duration="192000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="1,0" startTime="96000"  duration="192000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="2,0" startTime="0"      duration="192000"/>
    <!-- THE CROSSING SPLIT IS UNDONE TOO, which is why D4 (a) could choose a
         split: lane 3 is ONE clip again, at its own place. -->
    <assert-clip-window clip="3,0" startTime="240000" duration="192000"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="3,1" expectReject="true"/>
    <assert-clip-window clip="0,1" expectReject="true"/>

    <!-- Rebalanced for `verify-undo`, which compares undo and redo COUNTS. -->
    <redo count="7"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takes="2" duration="288000"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="3,0" takes="1" extents="240000-288000"/>

    <!-- ===== THE STAMP REACHED THE TAKE (plan 53 §8 P4, §6.5) =========== -->
    <!--
      `takeStamp="12:00"` above is what the recorder passes, and the plan turns
      it into a `set-clip-name` on the take it just made. Nothing can read a
      take's name back - there is no `assert-clip-name` verb - so it is
      asserted through the one thing that depends on it: a take added AFTER the
      pass, carrying no stamp, must NOT be what `newest` picks.

      Lane 0 then holds take 0 (the clip it was played against), take 1 (the
      pass, stamped) and take 2 (just added, unstamped and ACTIVE, since
      `add-take` activates). `newest` must answer 1. Both ways of getting this
      wrong land on 2: a stamp that never reached the take leaves nothing
      stamped at all and falls back to the last index, and a `newest` that
      ordered by index rather than by stamp picks the last index directly.

      broadcast="0": lanes 1-3 are this lane's twins and would each resolve
      `newest` against their own column, which `takes_group_broadcast` is where
      to assert. Here the claim is about one column's names.
    -->
    <add-take clip="0,0" filePath="../test_sawtooth.wav"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takes="3" activeTake="2"/>
    <select-take clip="0,0" take="newest" broadcast="0"/>
    <assert-take-column clip="0,0" takes="3" activeTake="1"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="5"/>
  </assertions>

  <verify-undo/>

</SActionScript>
